course: dictionary
lesson: 11028
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word way can mean different things, so the words around it tell you which meaning you need. «Which way is the station?» Here way means a road or direction to a place. «There is more than one way to solve this puzzle» uses way to mean a method, or how you do something.
explain: Way can also mean distance, as in «We still have a long way to go.» The clue is the word long, which tells you the distance is big. In «That soup is way too hot», way means very, so the sentence says the soup is very hot.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «way too hot» becomes «very too hot», that does not sound quite right, but «far too hot» does, so way here means very or far. Always test the meaning in the sentence before you decide.
fact: Way is a noun. It can mean a road, path or direction, or the way you do something.
fact: Way can also be an adverb meaning very or far, as in «way too big».
fact: Phrases like «by the way», «a long way», «on the way» and «give way» have their own meanings, so learn them as whole chunks.
fact: «By the way» adds something new to what you are talking about, as in «By the way, I found your pencil».
fact: Casual talk, such as «No way!», means I don't believe it, and it can also be a playful way to say no.
exercise: «Which way is the station?» What does way mean here? | A kind of hat | A method for cooking eggs | A very long time | * A road or direction to a place
exercise: «There is more than one way to solve this puzzle.» What does way mean here? | Very, or far | A road to school | The distance to the shop | * A method, or how you do something
exercise: «That soup is way too hot.» What does way mean here? | The distance to the shop | A method for cooking | A route to the kitchen | * Very, or far
test: «We still have a long way to go.» What does a long way mean? | A quick trip | A dangerous road | * A great distance | A lot of time
test: «By the way, I found your pencil.» What does by the way add to the talk? | A great distance | A road to the park | * Something new to the talk | A rude comment
exam: «No way!» said Mia when she heard the news. What does no way mean here? | We are going by bus | The road is closed | * I don't believe it | Mia is going home
